{
  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "All six completed experiments use singleprofile with no aggregation, leaving the multiprofile+aggregation dimension completely untested. The best result so far is config_016 (scvi_n200, resnet50, weighted, singleprofile; acc=0.540). The small multimodal gain over RNA-only (~1-2%) suggests the current single-profile setup may be underutilizing available information. config_028 directly extends the best configuration by switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while keeping the same encoders (scvi_n200, resnet50) and fusion (weighted). This isolates the effect of multiprofile+aggregation with the simplest, most robust aggregation method, avoiding the confound of simultaneously introducing a more complex transformer aggregator. If it improves on 0.540, we gain evidence that multi-profile information is valuable and can then explore transformer aggregation; if not, we learn that added complexity is not warranted, saving budget from pursuing that direction."
}

